# Media Query Conventions

## Standard Implementation

Always use the `mq-up` mixin for media queries targeting sizes larger than mobile. This ensures consistent breakpoint handling across the project.

**Important:** Ensure you import the mixins correctly in your SCSS file, typically with `@use "../../../scss/util/util-mixins" as mixins;` or a similar path.

### Correct Usage

```scss
.my-component {
    // Mobile-first styles here
    padding: 1rem;

    @include mixins.mq-up(lg) {
        // Styles for large screens and up
        padding: 2rem;
        font-size: 1.125rem;
    }
}
```

### Available Breakpoints
- xs: 0px (default, no media query needed)
- sm: 576px
- md: 768px
- lg: 992px
- xl: 1200px
- xxl: 1400px

### Common Patterns
#### Sticky Elements:

```scss
.sticky-sidebar {
    @include mixins.mq-up(lg) {
        position: sticky;
        top: 2rem;
        align-self: flex-start;
    }
}
```

#### Grid Layouts:

```scss
.card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;

    @include mixins.mq-up(md) {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    @include mixins.mq-up(lg) {
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
}
```

### ❌ Don't Use
Avoid using standard CSS media queries directly, as this bypasses the theme's managed breakpoints.

```scss
// ❌ Don't use standard media queries
@media (min-width: 992px) {
    // ...
}

// ❌ Don't use max-width queries unless absolutely necessary (breaks mobile-first)
@media (max-width: 768px) {
    // ...
}
```

### ✅ Do Use
Always structure your SCSS mobile-first and use `mq-up` to add styles for larger screens.

```scss
.component {
    // Mobile-first styles here
    color: var(--ts-color-primary, red);

    @include mixins.mq-up(md) {
        // Tablet and up styles
        color: var(--ts-color-secondary, blue);
    }

    @include mixins.mq-up(lg) {
        // Desktop and up styles
        color: var(--ts-color-primary-dark, black);
    }
}
```

## Best Practices
1. Always start with mobile styles (mobile-first approach).
2. Use the `mq-up` mixin for consistent breakpoint management.
3. Keep media queries organized within their component/block SCSS files.
4. Consider performance implications of complex styles added at larger breakpoints.
